.TITLE "grep"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Searches for patterns in text files using regular expressions. It filters __input data__ and displays lines that match specified criteria.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**egrep** **fgrep**

.DIV "TLDR"
**grep "pattern" file**
Searches for a specific pattern within a file.
> __"pattern"__ search term | __file__ target path

**grep -i "pattern" file**
Performs a case-insensitive search.
> __-i__ ignore case flag

**grep -v "pattern" file**
Displays only the lines that do not match the pattern.
> __-v__ invert match flag

**grep -r "pattern" directory**
Searches for a pattern recursively within all files in a directory.
> __-r__ recursive flag

**grep -E "pattern" file**
Uses extended regular expressions for more complex search patterns.
> __-E__ extended regex flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
On macOS, __grep__ follows BSD conventions. Using __grep -E__ is functionally equivalent to using the __egrep__ alias and is often preferred for modern scripts.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:find** **mac:sed**

